{"issue":{"base_status":"open","comments":[],"created_at":"2026-09-02T03:08:52.855477895Z","data":{},"dependencies":[{"blocker":"util-73916ac1","kind":"blocks"}],"description":"Plan: docs/plan/plan.md Phase 3 (b). Blocked by Phase 3a.\n\n## Task\n- `rules.yaml` shipped in the leaf and read from ~/.config/org-rule-guard/rules.yaml (XDG honoured):\n  one entry per rule with id, tools, patterns (regex), path globs where relevant, message, enabled.\n  Python keeps only the engine (input parsing, matching, deny output, logging).\n- The credential rule becomes a delegation to `agent-secrets/hooks/credential-guard.py` (import or\n  subprocess), so the two guards no longer carry duplicate pattern lists.\n- A malformed rules file fails open with one logged `rules_load_error` line, matching the hook contract.\n\n## Acceptance\n- The six default rules produce the same allow/deny decisions as Phase 3a on the same fixtures.\n- Adding a rule in YAML (no Python change) blocks a new fixture; disabling one allows it.\n- Documented so a promoted lesson (NEEDLE ADR-027) can land as a YAML entry under review.","external_references":[],"id":"util-50917f2f","issue_type":"task","labels":["factory-learning","org-rule-guard"],"manual_blocked":false,"notes":"","priority":2,"profile":"native-v1","revision":1,"schema_ref":"urn:bead-rs:schema:issue:native-v1","title":"org-rule-guard: move rules to ~/.config/org-rule-guard/rules.yaml and delegate the credential rule to credential-guard (Phase 3b)","updated_at":"2026-09-02T03:08:52.855477895Z"},"record_type":"issue"}
{"issue":{"base_status":"open","comments":[],"created_at":"2026-09-02T03:08:52.763589875Z","data":{},"description":"Plan: docs/plan/plan.md Phase 3 (a). Companion to NEEDLE plan section 4.4 (operator-side loop).\n\n## Why\nThe org-wide PreToolUse guard at ~/.claude/hooks/org-rule-guard.py (332 lines, six rules) has exactly\none output path: the deny JSON on stdout. Nothing records which rule fired, in which repo, how often.\nThe enforcement layer emits no learning signal, so CLAUDE.md prose cannot be tuned against evidence.\n\n## Task\n1. Create utilities/org-rule-guard/ as a leaf: hooks/org-rule-guard.py (ported from the live hook,\n   same six rules, same fail-open contract), hooks/test_org_rule_guard.py (one allow and one deny\n   fixture per rule, built at runtime so no rule-triggering literal sits in the test file), install.sh\n   (idempotent copy into ~/.claude/hooks/; edits settings.json only with --wire), README.md, VERSION.\n2. On every deny, append one JSON line to ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/org-rule-guard/denials.jsonl:\n   ts (UTC ISO-8601), rule_id (stable slug), tool, cwd, session_id (from the hook input if present), and\n   a redacted 80-char fragment of what matched. For the credential rule the fragment is the pattern\n   name only; never a value. Directory mode 700. Logging failures never change the decision.\n3. README: log format plus a jq recipe for \"denials by rule_id, last 7 days\".\n\n## Acceptance\n- Test suite passes against both the live hook and the ported copy on the same fixtures.\n- A deny writes exactly one line; an allow writes nothing.\n- install.sh without --wire does not touch ~/.claude/settings.json or overwrite an existing hook file.","external_references":[],"id":"util-73916ac1","issue_type":"task","labels":["deferred","factory-learning","failure-count:3","org-rule-guard","verification-failed"],"manual_blocked":false,"notes":"Duplicate dispatch: a prior session on this bead shipped and pushed 09c4841 + a878e20 at 09:21-09:23 while this session was independently verifying the same work; its tree is byte-identical to what it committed, so nothing was rebuilt. This session verified the shipped state instead of duplicating it: 35 tests green against the ported copy and 35 run/15 log tests skipped green against ~/.claude/hooks/org-rule-guard.py on the same fixtures (ORG_RULE_GUARD_UNDER_TEST); a deny appends exactly one JSONL line (ts/rule_id/tool/cwd/session_id/fragment) and an allow appends nothing and stays silent at exit 0; state dir 700 and file 600 via a single O_APPEND write; the credential rule logs its pattern name only and a runtime-built fake ghp_ token appears nowhere in the log, including on a mixed command where the credential rule wins ordering; bare install.sh against the real HOME left the live hook sha256-identical and ~/.claude/settings.json untouched; the README jq recipe was checked against a synthetic log holding 1/3/10/20-day-old records and correctly counts only the 7-day window; and a live-vs-ported comparison over 8 allow/deny cases matched on every decision with byte-equal deny reasons. Also fixed the stale plan Components section (9233117, pushed) which still described the hook as planned and reading rules from a rules.yaml that is 3(b), and tagged org-rule-guard/v0.1.0 at 09c4841 per the documented per-utility tag convention.","priority":1,"profile":"native-v1","revision":17,"schema_ref":"urn:bead-rs:schema:issue:native-v1","title":"org-rule-guard: extract the hook into utilities and append a JSONL record for every denial (Phase 3a)","updated_at":"2026-09-05T13:49:47.231000909Z"},"record_type":"issue"}
